# ScamShield AI — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` if you want to keep these in one place, but note: the app reads the *process
# environment*, not this file. Export the variables in your shell (or set them in your launcher)
# before starting:
#   PowerShell:  $env:SCAMSHIELD_MODEL = "gemma4:e2b"
#   bash/zsh:    export SCAMSHIELD_MODEL=gemma4:e2b
#
# There are no API keys, tokens or secrets in this project. Everything runs on this machine, and
# nothing is uploaded. Do not commit a real `.env`; this template is the only env file in git.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local model server
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where Ollama listens. Change only if you moved it off the default port.
OLLAMA_HOST=http://127.0.0.1:11434

# Force a specific installed model instead of auto-picking from PREFERRED_MODELS.
# Default choice is Gemma 4 E2B (~3.5 GB download, fits an 8 GB CPU laptop).
# Larger options on a machine with more RAM: gemma4:e4b, gemma4:26b-a4b
SCAMSHIELD_MODEL=gemma4:e2b

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local storage
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite file for learning + scan history. Defaults to <repo>/data/scamshield.db.
# Tests override this to a temporary file, so do not point it at a shared location.
# SCAMSHIELD_DB=./data/scamshield.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not used by this project (listed to prevent confusion)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No cloud LLM keys (OPENAI_API_KEY, GEMINI_API_KEY …) — the app never calls a hosted model.
# No database URL — SQLite is a local file, see DATABASE.md.
# No auth secrets — the app binds to 127.0.0.1 and has no accounts.
